**Review of the provider-scoped model RED test (72 pass, 1 fail)**

The test is well-designed. The fix requires `getModelItems` to know the already-accepted `--provider` value so it can filter. 

Cleanest approach per the plan's single-scanner principle: have `analyzeArgumentCursor` capture the provider value during its scan (it already processes `--provider <value>` tokens and adds "provider" to `usedSemanticIds`). Extend the cursor expectation to carry `parsedProviderValue: string | undefined`, then thread it through `getSuggestions` to `getModelItems`.

Alternative (less clean): re-parse the whole line in `getSuggestions` to extract the provider. This violates the plan's "no candidate-specific reparsing" constraint.

One design note: the `ValueCursorExpectation` type could carry a `parsedValues: Map<string, string>` (or just `parsedProviderValue`) from the scan. Since the scanner already reads option values, this is a minimal extension — just stash the provider value when `option.semanticId === "provider"` during the scan.

