[from reviewer on team agent-autocomplete-completion]
**Review of mid-line async chaining fix — no issues found.**

The `observeChainedOptionEdit` approach is sound:
- 500ms deadline prevents unbounded polling.
- Three clean stop conditions: (1) expected value position reached → triggers value menu, (2) autocomplete already showing → defers to Pi, (3) deadline exceeded → stops silently.
- `semanticId` check ensures chaining targets the right option, not a stale or different edit.
- `pendingChainedOption` guard correctly gates on: no picker showing + Tab/Enter + single matching option + has completion domain. This precisely identifies the Pi "unique forced completion" case.

The `acceptedChainedOption` simplification from individual domain checks to `completionDomain !== undefined` is correct — free-form options (`tools`, `exclude-tools`, `system-prompt`, `append-system-prompt`) all have `completionDomain: undefined` and correctly won't chain.

`triggerValueAutocomplete` extraction is clean — consolidates path vs non-path in one place.

79/0 confirmed. The useless escape at line 169 is still pending.

